From: W1700K MLO maintenance
Subject: [PATCH] luci-base: avoid constructing a wireless device without a name

Against LuCI 289a7260434d4b8212a9cc6cf6160cb1935270c1.
A wifi-iface with a list-valued device has no synthetic netid in this
version. If its runtime section exists without an interface name,
WifiNetwork.getDevice() constructs Device(undefined). Rendering the
wireless signal badge calls isUp(), then Device.getType(), which throws
at this.device.indexOf('.'). This path predates the 0004 view guards.

Return null when there is no device name, as the existing WifiNetwork
isUp() null check expects. Keep scalar network IDs and runtime MLO names
unchanged. This does not implement multi-radio synthetic IDs.

The captured r44 status includes ap-mld0 and does not reproduce the error;
the host regression deliberately removes the runtime interface name.
Do not treat this hardening as proof of the live incident's root cause.
Pin the package version/revision so the working-tree patch is visible.

--- a/modules/luci-base/Makefile
+++ b/modules/luci-base/Makefile
@@ -7,6 +7,8 @@
 include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=luci-base
+PKG_VERSION:=26.253.65031~289a726
+PKG_RELEASE:=2
 PKG_BUILD_FLAGS:=no-lto
 
 LUCI_TYPE:=mod
--- a/modules/luci-base/htdocs/luci-static/resources/network.js
+++ b/modules/luci-base/htdocs/luci-static/resources/network.js
@@ -4480,12 +4480,14 @@ WifiNetwork = baseclass.extend(/** @lends LuCI.network.WifiNetwork.prototype */ {
 	/**
 	 * Get the associated Linux network device.
 	 *
-	 * @returns {LuCI.network.Device}
+	 * @returns {null|LuCI.network.Device}
 	 * Returns a `Network.Device` instance representing the Linux network
-	 * device associated with this wireless network.
+	 * device associated with this wireless network, or `null` if no device
+	 * name can be resolved.
 	 */
 	getDevice() {
-		return Network.prototype.instantiateDevice(this.getIfname());
+		const ifname = this.getIfname();
+		return ifname != null ? Network.prototype.instantiateDevice(ifname) : null;
 	},
 
 	/**
